The problem with leaving pets weapons is that it is a waste...

When a creature becomes your pet, it obeys the standard pet rules:
e.g. 
1) Doesn't walk on cursed items,
2) Picks up AND drops objects.
etc

Point 2 is important, because although your Marilith will happily pick
up your +8 Frostbrand, it will undoubtedly drop it within the next turn or
so... :-(

This is a byt of a downer:-)

Also the Dev team, by bug or feature, have limited pets grossness.
Although their Max hitpoints will tend towards infinity given enough time,
if it's hitpoints are above approx. 130hp, and the monster gets hit, it
will knock it's hp to 130. This means that a Balrog with 800hp has really
only 130 or so...:-(

Another byt of a downer:-)

Oh well! that's enough grossness:-)

